From: William Mangum <william@wsds.io>
Subject: [PATCH] egl/dri2: no EGL_WL_bind_wayland_display without a device name

A software GBM device (GBM_ALWAYS_SOFTWARE=1, or a card without a render
node such as bochs-drm, simpledrm and hyperv_drm) has no render fd:
dri2_initialize_drm never sets fd_render_gpu for it, so
loader_get_device_name_for_fd() returns NULL and device_name stays unset,
while EGL_WL_bind_wayland_display is still advertised from the PRIME caps
of the card. The name is what eglBindWaylandDisplayWL hands wl_drm clients;
a client that calls it (WPEBackend-fdo does, ahead of its linux-dmabuf and
wl_shm paths) crashed inside strdup(NULL). Advertise the extension only
with a device name, and never strdup a missing one.

Upstream: not yet submitted (embraOS carries this until it is).
Signed-off-by: William Mangum <william@wsds.io>
---
 src/egl/drivers/dri2/egl_dri2.c     | 2 +-
 src/egl/drivers/dri2/platform_drm.c | 6 +++++-
 2 files changed, 6 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/src/egl/drivers/dri2/egl_dri2.c
+++ b/src/egl/drivers/dri2/egl_dri2.c
@@ -2696,7 +2696,7 @@ dri2_bind_wayland_display_wl(_EGLDisplay *disp, struct wl_display *wl_dpy)
       goto fail;
 
    device_name = drmGetRenderDeviceNameFromFd(dri2_dpy->fd_render_gpu);
-   if (!device_name)
+   if (!device_name && dri2_dpy->device_name)
       device_name = strdup(dri2_dpy->device_name);
    if (!device_name)
       goto fail;
--- a/src/egl/drivers/dri2/platform_drm.c
+++ b/src/egl/drivers/dri2/platform_drm.c
@@ -712,7 +712,11 @@ dri2_initialize_drm(_EGLDisplay *disp)
    dri2_dpy->device_name =
       loader_get_device_name_for_fd(dri2_dpy->fd_render_gpu);
 #endif
-   dri2_set_WL_bind_wayland_display(disp);
+   /* A software device has no render fd and so no device name, and the
+    * name is what eglBindWaylandDisplayWL hands wl_drm clients: without
+    * one the extension cannot be served and is not advertised. */
+   if (dri2_dpy->device_name)
+      dri2_set_WL_bind_wayland_display(disp);
 
    /* Fill vtbl last to prevent accidentally calling virtual function during
     * initialization.
